  "discussion": "Fresh trade winds will continue through Tuesday as a front quickly approaches from the northwest. Trade winds will oveerun this weakening feature and wind speeds will strengthen again Tuesday night. The remnant trough will move in Thursday, spreading clouds and showers across the coastal waters. A northwest swell will continue through Tuesday night and keep moderate surf in the forecast along north and west facing shores. A much larger northwest to north-northwest swell was generated by a gale force low developing east of Kamchatka. This large north- northwest swell may bring warning level surf heights to exposed north and west facing shores building in through the day on Wednesday, peaking Wednesday night, decreasing to advisory levels on Thursday, and then falling below advisory levels by Friday. A small northwest reinforecement is expected to arrive this weekend. Surf along east facing shores will decrease as winds taper through Tuesday, but will ramp up again by Wednesday through Friday as wind speeds pick back up. A small south swell will decline through the week.",
